-- title:
--   Realisation of finite idele classes by cyclic N-isogenies
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points $P$ with $q'\cdot P=0$ vanish. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, that is, it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is not properly contained in any such submodule; let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₁`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) of $\mathrm{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the additive maps which are $0$ or given by a pair of rational functions off a finite set, with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\neq 0$ be a natural number with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $m$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ both lie in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ₁`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) (the additive group generated by $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele), such that [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ₁ m`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $=\mathbb{H}\cap m\widehat{\Lambda}_1m^{-1}$ is again a maximal order, and such that $R=\Lambda_1\sqcap\mathbb{H}\cap m\widehat{\Lambda}_1m^{-1}$ has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups. Then for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ there are: an elliptic curve $W/\kappa$, a nonzero additive map $\chi\colon X_1(\kappa)\to W(\kappa)$ lying in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ X₁ W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, such that $\theta_1$ carries the set of elements of `rationalEndSubring κ X₁` of the form $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho$ a rational homomorphism $W\to X_1$ onto the image under quaternion conjugation of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}_1)$; and, for the same $d$, an elliptic curve $W'/\kappa$ together with rational homomorphisms $\psi\colon W\to W'$ and $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ satisfying $\psi'\circ\psi=N$ and $\psi\circ\psi'=N$ and such that $\theta_1$ carries the corresponding kernel-ideal set of $\psi\circ\chi$ onto the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap xm\widehat{\Lambda}_1)$; and the kernel of $\psi$ is cyclic of cardinality $N$.
--
--   This is the Deuring–Eichler dictionary in its level-$N$ form: the class of a finite idele $x$ for the Eichler order $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda}_1m^{-1}$ of index $N$ corresponds to a cyclic $N$-isogeny $W\to W'$ between the supersingular curves attached to the $\Lambda_1$-classes of $x$ and of $xm$, with the kernel-ideal description of $\mathrm{Hom}$-modules transported along $\theta_1$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the supersingular points and the Atkin–Lehner action on the places of the modular curve of level divisible by $q'$.
